sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Frontend
    participant Express as Express.js<br/>Auth Service
    participant MongoDB
    participant EmailService

    User->>Frontend: 1. Fill Registration Form<br/>(username, email, password, role, location)
    Frontend->>Frontend: 2. Validate Input<br/>(password strength, format)
    
    alt Validation Fails
        Frontend->>User: Show Error (Invalid Input)
    else Validation Passes
        Frontend->>Express: 3. POST /auth/register<br/>(credentials + role)
        Express->>Express: 4. Hash Password<br/>(bcryptjs)
        Express->>MongoDB: 5. Create User Document<br/>(with role-specific fields)
        MongoDB-->>Express: User Created
        Express->>EmailService: 6. Send Verification Email<br/>(with token)
        EmailService-->>User: Verification Email
        Express-->>Frontend: 7. Return Success<br/>(+ session info)
        Frontend->>User: Show "Check Email" Page
    end

    User->>EmailService: 8. Click Verification Link
    EmailService->>Express: 9. GET /auth/verify?token=xyz
    Express->>MongoDB: 10. Find & Update User<br/>(isEmailVerified: true)
    MongoDB-->>Express: Updated
    Express-->>User: 11. Redirect to Login<br/>Success Message

    User->>Frontend: 12. Login Page<br/>(email + password)
    Frontend->>Express: 13. POST /auth/login
    Express->>MongoDB: 14. Find User by Email
    MongoDB-->>Express: User Document
    Express->>Express: 15. Compare Password Hash
    
    alt Password Incorrect
        Express-->>Frontend: 16. Return Error
        Frontend->>User: "Invalid Credentials"
    else Password Correct
        Express->>Express: 17. Generate JWT Token
        Express-->>Frontend: 18. Return JWT + User Data
        Frontend->>Frontend: 19. Store JWT in localStorage
        Frontend->>User: 20. Redirect to Dashboard
    end